ai-orchestrator adaptations (2026-08-22): the architecture is upstream's — the
slot-formatted pattern catalogue, the "what not to flag" guard, the
do-not-invent-facts rule, the prose-only fence, and the two-question second pass.
The content is not. Upstream's 35 patterns target English prose and were measured
against this repository before being carried over:

  - Its lexical patterns (§1-8 content, §23-24 filler) found 4 hits in ~20,000
    comment lines. Dropped: nothing to act on.
  - Its style patterns (§9 "not X but Y", §14 em-dashes, §15-16 bold and bold
    mini-headings) found 3,795 hits — and DESIGN.md#writing mandates every one of
    those shapes. Inverted into "What not to touch", where they now protect the
    house voice instead of flagging it.
  - §2 (name-dropping to prove importance) transferred nearly verbatim as P2.

The six patterns that remain were derived by scanning this repository's own 1,080
comment blocks. Upstream's file mode became scope-from-the-caller so a loop can
pass a diff, and the prose-only fence became a script that proves it.
